{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792604777,"nonce":"7DAgcnLfM51AE1gw011CcA8pltI=","title":"Check discarded branches and method callbacks consistently","message":"RayDE src/rayde/ext/BridgeControl.hx buildCanvas uses an if as a statement. Its scrolling branch ends in Interaction.onClick, returning Interaction; the other branch calls fill, returning Void. The LSP post-typing pass incorrectly requires those discarded branch results to match, producing expected Interaction, found Void at the if.\n\nThe method-call checker also uses a separate exact-type-only signature matcher. Compatible callback aliases and independently constructed function types fail there; diagnostics then compare the method type to itself, printing identical expected and found signatures.\n\nTrack statement/value use while checking conditionals, including nested blocks, metadata and loops. Keep checks on branch contents, conditions and conditional values. Use the common compatibility checker for methods and overloads, and report the actual failing argument.\n\nValidation includes real LSP protocol tests for fluent/Void branches, nested conditionals, invalid conditions and calls, incompatible conditional values, valid callback aliases with discarded return values, and incompatible callback parameter types.\n\nThe editor post-check also lacked registered inheritance edges for imported typed classes. Populate the existing ClassHierarchyBuilder from the shared compiled graph before checking the active file; cover a child-to-base assignment through an imported intermediate class.","files":null}]}